<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2010/07/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>VL.GIS</id>
    <!--
      Prerelease on purpose. nuget.org hides prerelease versions from default search and
      vvvv needs an explicit opt-in to install one, which enforces "not for real projects"
      mechanically rather than relying on anyone reading the description.
      Drop the -alpha once the nodes have actually been exercised.
    -->
    <version>0.1.0-alpha</version>
    <title>VL.GIS — GIS Library for vvvv gamma</title>
    <authors>VL.GIS Contributors</authors>
    <owners>VL.GIS Contributors</owners>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <license type="expression">MIT</license>
    <readme>docs\README.md</readme>
    <projectUrl>https://github.com/lavalse/vvvv-gis</projectUrl>
    <description>
      EARLY AND LARGELY UNTESTED - please do not use this in a real project yet.

      What is verified: the package installs and its nodes appear in the NodeBrowser.
      What is NOT verified: the GIS functionality itself. Almost none of the nodes have
      been run. There are no help patches and no tests. Node names and categories will
      change between releases. Bug reports and PRs welcome.

      Geographic Information System (GIS) library for vvvv gamma.

      Provides nodes for:
      - GIS.Geometry: create and manipulate Points, Lines, Polygons (NetTopologySuite)
      - GIS.Projection: reproject between CRS (ProjNet; EPSG:4326, EPSG:3857, UTM)
      - GIS.Serialization: parse/write WKT, WKB, GeoJSON
      - GIS.Tiles: fetch map tiles from OSM and XYZ sources (BruTile)
      - GIS.Mesh: local coordinates, polygon tessellation, heightmaps

      Requires vvvv gamma 7.2 or newer (.NET 8).
    </description>
    <summary>GIS geometry, projection, serialization, map tiles and mesh nodes for vvvv gamma.</summary>
    <releaseNotes>
      0.1.0-alpha - First release whose nodes actually appear in vvvv.

      The 0.0.x line (0.0.1 - 0.0.4, now unlisted) installed and contributed no nodes at
      all, for three independent reasons, none of which produced an error message:
      malformed document IDs in VL.GIS.vl (VL requires exactly 22 characters, first in
      [A-V]); a missing UTF-8 BOM; and no [assembly: ImportAsIs] on the forwarded
      assemblies, without which their public statics are demoted to raw .NET reflection
      nodes that the NodeBrowser hides.

      The entry point is now generated rather than hand-written, and all three failure
      modes are asserted before release.

      Also in this release: node categories are GIS.Geometry / GIS.Projection /
      GIS.Serialization / GIS.Tiles / GIS.Mesh.*; VL.GIS.Stride is renamed VL.GIS.Mesh
      since it never referenced Stride; minimum vvvv version is now gamma 7.2.

      The GIS functionality itself remains essentially untested - see the README.
    </releaseNotes>
    <copyright>Copyright 2026 VL.GIS Contributors</copyright>
    <!-- The "VL" tag is what makes the pack discoverable at https://vvvv.org/packs -->
    <tags>VL vvvv gamma gis geospatial geography map projection geometry</tags>
    <repository type="git" url="https://github.com/lavalse/vvvv-gis" />

    <!--
      VL.CoreLib is deliberately absent: it ships with vvvv itself, so packages must not
      declare it here (matches VL.OpenCV / VL.Devices.RealSense / VL.HardwareMonitor).
      It is declared in VL.GIS.vl as a <NugetDependency> instead, which is what makes its
      nodes visible.
    -->
    <!-- System.Reactive is deliberately absent too: vvvv ships 6.0.0 and logs
         "wasn't picked up because it's provided by vvvv itself" for anything we pin. -->
    <dependencies>
      <group targetFramework="net8.0">
        <dependency id="NetTopologySuite"            version="2.6.0" />
        <dependency id="NetTopologySuite.IO.GeoJSON" version="3.0.0" />
        <dependency id="ProjNet"                     version="2.1.0" />
        <dependency id="BruTile"                     version="6.0.0" />
      </group>
    </dependencies>
  </metadata>

  <files>
    <!-- Entry point. Must sit at the package root, no subfolder. -->
    <file src="VL.GIS.vl" target="" />

    <file src="src\VL.GIS.Core\bin\Release\net8.0\VL.GIS.Core.dll"  target="lib\net8.0\" />
    <file src="src\VL.GIS.Core\bin\Release\net8.0\VL.GIS.Core.xml"  target="lib\net8.0\" />
    <file src="src\VL.GIS.Tiles\bin\Release\net8.0\VL.GIS.Tiles.dll" target="lib\net8.0\" />
    <file src="src\VL.GIS.Tiles\bin\Release\net8.0\VL.GIS.Tiles.xml" target="lib\net8.0\" />
    <file src="src\VL.GIS.Mesh\bin\Release\net8.0\VL.GIS.Mesh.dll"   target="lib\net8.0\" />
    <file src="src\VL.GIS.Mesh\bin\Release\net8.0\VL.GIS.Mesh.xml"   target="lib\net8.0\" />

    <file src="help\**\*.vl" target="help\" />

    <!-- Shown on the nuget.org listing page. -->
    <file src="README.md"               target="docs\" />
    <file src="THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md"  target="docs\" />
    <!-- LICENSE is not packed: <license type="expression">MIT</license> above is what
         nuget.org displays, and the extensionless filename makes nuget read any target
         as a directory name, producing docs\LICENSE.txt\LICENSE. -->

  </files>
</package>
